 nozzle temperature control detected; the heating module may be damaged. Please disconnect the power immediately and stop using the device, and contact customer support for troubleshooting...␀The nozzle temperature is abnormal; the sensor may have a short circuit. Please check whether the connector is properly plugged in.␀The nozzle temperature is abnormal; the sensor may have an open circuit.␀Nozzle temperature control is abnormal. The hot end may not be installed. To heat the heating assembly without the hotend, enable Maintenance Mode.␀The hotend cooling fan speed is too slow or stopped. It may be stuck or the connector may not be plugged in properly.␀The hotend cooling fan is running slowly. It may be obstructed. Please check for debris and clean if necessary.␀The speed of the part cooling fan is too slow or stopped. It may be stuck, or the connector may not be plugged in properly.␀The motor driver is overheating. Its radiator may be loose, or its cooling fan may be damaged.␀Motor-A has an open-circuit. There may be a loose connection, or the motor may have failed.␀Motor-A has a short-circuit. It may have failed.␀The resistance of Motor-A is abnormal; the motor may have failed.␀Motor-B has an open-circuit. The connection may be loose, or the motor may have failed.␀Motor-B has a short-circuit. It may have failed.␀The resistance of Motor-B is abnormal; the motor may have failed.␀Motor-Z has an open-circuit. The connection may be loose, or the motor may have failed.␀Motor-Z has a short-circuit. It may have failed.␀The resistance of Motor-Z is abnormal; the motor may have failed.␀The extruder servo motor has an open circuit. The connection may be loose, or the motor may have failed.␀The extruder servo motor has a short-circuit. It may have failed.␀The resistance of the extruder servo motor is abnormal; the motor may have failed.␀Heatbed force sensor 1 is too sensitive. It may be stuck between the strain arm and heatbed support, or the adjusting screw may be too tight.␀The signal of heatbed force sensor 1 is weak. The force sensor may be broken or have poor electric connection.␀The signal of heatbed force sensor 1 is too weak. The electronic connection to the sensor may be broken.␀An external disturbance was detected on force sensor 1. The heatbed plate may have touched something outside the heatbed.␀Force sensor 1 detected unexpected continuous force. The heatbed may be stuck, or the analog front end may be broken.␀Heatbed force sensor 2 is too sensitive. It may be stuck between the strain arm and heatbed support, or the adjusting screw may be too tight.␀The signal of heatbed force sensor 2 is weak. The force sensor may be broken or have poor electric connection.␀The signal of heatbed force sensor 2 is too weak. The electronic connection to the sensor may be broken.␀An external disturbance was detected on force sensor 2. The heatbed plate may have touched something outside the heatbed.␀Force sensor 2 detected unexpected continuous force. The heatbed may be stuck, or the analog front end may be broken.␀Heatbed force sensor 3 is too sensitive. It may be stuck between the strain arm and heatbed support, or the adjusting screw may be too tight.␀The signal of heatbed force sensor 3 is weak. The force sensor may be broken or have poor electric connection.␀The signal of heatbed force sensor 3 is too weak. The electronic connection to the sensor may be broken.␀An external disturbance was detected on force sensor 3. The heatbed plate may have touched something outside the heatbed.␀Force sensor 3 detected unexpected continuous force. The heatbed may be stuck, or the analog front end may be broken.␀Heatbed homing failed. The environmental vibration is too great.␀The build plate is not placed properly. Please adjust it.␀The Z axis motor seems to be stuck when moving. Please check if there is any foreign matter on the Z sliders or Z timing belt wheels.␀The heatbed leveling data is abnormal. Please check whether there are any foreign objects on the heatbed and Z slider. If so, please remove them and try again.␀Heatbed homing abnormal: there may be a bulge on the heatbed or the nozzle tip may not be clean.␀The build plate may not be properly placed. If this message appears repeatedly, please check the Wiki for more explanations.␀Abnormal accelerometer data detected. Please try restarting the printer.␀The resonance frequency of the X axis is low. The timing belt may be loose.␀The resonance frequency of the X-axis differs significantly from the last calibration. Please clean the carbon rod and conduct a calibration after printing.␀The resonance frequency of the Y axis is low. The timing belt may be loose.␀The resonance frequency of the Y-axis differs greatly from the last calibration. Please clean the Y-axis liner rod and conduct a calibration after printing.␀The front cover of the toolhead fell off.␀The current sensor of Motor-A is abnormal. This may be caused by a failure of the hardware sampling circuit.␀The current sensor of Motor-B is abnormal. This may be caused by a failure of the hardware sampling circuit.␀The current sensor of Motor-Z is abnormal. This may be caused by a failure of the hardware sampling circuit.␀The extruder servo motor's current sensor is abnormal. A failure of the hardware sampling circuit may cause this.␀The hotend cooling fan speed is slow. It may be stuck and need cleaning.␀The nozzle is covered with filament, or the build plate is crooked.␀The nozzle is clogged with filament.␀The signal of the heatbed acceleration sensor is weak. The sensor may have fallen off or been damaged.␀External disturbance was detected on the heatbed acceleeration sensor. The sensor signal wire may not be affixed.␀The heatbed acceleration sensor detected unexpected continuous force. The sensor may be stuck, or the analog front end may be broken.␀The extrusion motor driver is abnormal. The MOSFET may have a short circuit.␀X-axis homing abnormal: please check if the toolhead is stuck or the carbon rod resistance is too high.␀Y-axis homing abnormal: please check if the toolhead is stuck or the Y carriage has too much resistance.␀X axis homing abnormal: the timing belt may be loose.␀Y axis homing abnormal: the timing belt may be loose.␀Data transmission over the serial port is abnormal; the software system may be faulty.␀G-code data error detected. The system has automatically reloaded the G-code and resumed printing.␀Sliced file abnormality detected multiple times. Task canceled. Please check the sliced file.␀G-code verification error. The system has automatically reacquired the data and resumed printing.␀The system voltage is unstable. Triggering the power failure protection function.␀Chamber heating failed. The heater may not be blowing hot air.␀Chamber heating failed. Possible causes: the chamber is not fully enclosed, ambient temperature is too low, or the power supply heat dissipation vent is blocked.␀Chamber heating failed. The power supply temperature may be too high.␀Chamber heating failed. The speed of the heating fan is too low.␀Chamber heating failed. The thermal resistance is too high.␀High chamber temperature detected. If the hotend is overheating or emitting smoke, immediately power off the printer. Please refer to the Wiki for detailed troubleshooting instructions.␀The communication of chamber temperature controller is abnormal.␀Chamber temperature is abnormal. The chamber heater's temperature sensor may have a short circuit.␀Chamber temperature is abnormal. The chamber heater's temperature sensor may have an open circuit.␀Chamber temperature is abnormal. The chamber heater's temperature sensor at the air outlet may have a short circuit.␀Chamber temperature is abnormal. The chamber heater's temperature sensor at the air outlet may have an open circuit.␀Chamber temperature is abnormal. The temperature sensor at the power supply may have a short circuit.␀Chamber temperature is abnormal. The temperature sensor at power supply may have an open circuit.␀Chamber failed to reach the desired temperature. The machine will stop waiting for the chamber temperature.␀Chamber cooling may be too slow. You can open the front door or top cover to help cooling if the air in the chamber is non-toxic.␀Chamber temperature setting value exceed the limit, the boundary value will be set.␀The front door Hall sensor is abnormal; please check whether the connection wire is loose.␀The media pipeline is malfunctioning. Please restart the printer. If multiple attempts fail, please contact customer support.␀Live View camera is not connected. Please check the hardware and cable connections.␀Not enough space on MicroSD Card. Video recording and timelapse recording cannot be performed. Please clear some space.␀The Micro SD card is in Read-Only mode. Video recording and Timelapse recording cannot be performed. Please refer to the Wiki for assistance.␀Unformatted MicroSD Card: please format it.␀No MicroSD card detected. The liveview camera cannot record a time-lapse.␀Failed to connect to the internet. Please check the network connection.␀Device login failed; please check your account information.␀Failed to connect to the internet; please check the network connection.␀Unauthorized user: please check your account information.␀Streaming function error. Please check the network and try again. You can restart or update the printer if the issue persists.␀Liveview service login failed; please check your network connection.␀Time synchronization failed␀The MC module is malfunctioning; please restart the device or check device cable connection.␀The toolhead is malfunctioning. Please restart the device.␀The AMS module is malfunctioning. Please restart the device.␀The Filament Buffer module is malfunctioning. Please restart the device.␀Internal service is malfunctioning. Please restart the device.␀A system panic occurred. Please restart the device.␀A system hang occurred. Please restart the device.␀A system hang occurred. It has been recovered by automatic restart.␀System state is abnormal; please restore to factory settings.␀The screen is malfunctioning; please restart the device.␀Some external modules are incompatible with the printer's firmware version, which may affect normal operation. Please go to the "Firmware" page while connected to the internet to upgrade.␀Hardware incompatible; please check the Micro Lidar.␀The Chamber Temperature Controller module is malfunctioning. Please restart the device.␀The current firmware version is abnormal and printing cannot start. Please ensure the printer is connected to the network and go to the "Firmware" page to update.␀Wireless hardware error: please turn off/on WiFi or restart the device.␀The SD Card controller is malfunctioning.␀Some modules are incompatible with the printer's firmware version, which may affect use. Please go to the "Firmware" page to update after connected to the internet, or you may update offline...␀Micro SD Card capacity is insufficient to cache print files.␀User information has expired; please log in again.␀MicroSD Card performance degradation has been detected. It may affect print jobs, logs, and video records. Please format or change the MicroSD card.␀Failed to download print job; please check your network connection.␀Failed to report print state; please check your network connection.␀The content of print file is unreadable; please resend the print job.␀The print file is unauthorized.␀Failed to resume previous print.␀The firmware of AMS A does not match the printer. Please upgrade it on the "Firmware" page.␀Communication error detected with AMS, AMS lite or AMS HT. Please reconnect the module cable or restart the printer when it is idle.␀The bed temperature exceeds the filament's vitrification temperature, which may cause a nozzle clog. Please keep the front door of the printer open or lower the bed temperature.␀The RFID-tag on AMS A Slot1 cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS A Slot2 cannot be identified.␀The RFID-tag on AMS A Slot3 cannot 